#N canvas 40 60 1280 760 12;
#X declare -path ..;
#X obj 0 0 cnv 1 1280 46 empty empty example\ \ \ spiking\ drum\ machine\ \ -\ \ two\ Izhikevich\ neurons\ play\ a\ groove 14 23 0 20 #1d3557 #ffffff 0;
#X obj 1110 730 declare -path ..;
#X text 800 730 finds the nn.* objects one folder up ->, f 42;
#X text 20 730 neuralplay - Moisés Horta Valenzuela / SEMILLA.AI Studio, f 70;
#X text 20 56 Two spiking neurons as drummers. A slowly breathing current makes the regular-spiking neuron (kick) speed up and slow down \, a chattering neuron plays bursts on the hi-hat. Spikes trigger the sounds - no sequencer \, no clock. Built from [nn.izh~] (lesson 10)., f 175;
#X obj 10 96 cnv 1 680 554 empty empty THE\ TWO\ NEURONS 8 12 0 13 #e3f0fb #1d3557 0;
#X obj 30 136 hsl 160 15 0.02 2 1 1 empty empty breathing\ LFO\ rate\ (Hz) 0 -8 0 11 #fcfcfc #000000 #000000 5600 1;
#X floatatom 198 135 7 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X obj 30 162 osc~;
#X obj 30 188 *~ 4;
#X obj 30 214 +~ 9;
#X text 100 162 <- the kick current breathes: 9 +/- 4, f 22;
#X obj 30 252 nn.izh~ RS;
#X obj 130 214 r \$0-kick;
#X obj 110 290 s~ \$0-kickspk;
#X obj 30 320 nn.scope~ 48000;
#X text 30 428 KICK: regular spiking (RS) \, 1 s of membrane voltage. Spikes go to [s~ \$0-kickspk]., f 32;
#X text 370 162 the hat current is a constant 8: chattering neurons burst on their own, f 36;
#X obj 370 252 nn.izh~ CH;
#X obj 370 214 sig~ 8;
#X obj 450 214 r \$0-hat;
#X obj 450 290 s~ \$0-hatspk;
#X obj 370 320 nn.scope~ 48000;
#X text 370 428 HAT: chattering (CH) \, bursts of fast spikes. Spikes go to [s~ \$0-hatspk]., f 32;
#X obj 30 500 hsl 200 15 300 4000 1 1 empty exdrum-speed speed:\ neuron-ms\ per\ second\ (both) 0 -8 0 11 #fcfcfc #000000 #000000 9200 1;
#X floatatom 238 499 7 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 30 526 rate \$1;
#X obj 30 552 t a a;
#X obj 30 578 s \$0-kick;
#X obj 120 578 s \$0-hat;
#X msg 370 500 RS;
#X msg 406 500 IB;
#X msg 442 500 CH;
#X msg 478 500 FS;
#X obj 370 534 s \$0-kick;
#X text 370 564 <- other firing patterns for the kick (lesson 10), f 34;
#X text 30 604 TRY: speed 3000 = frantic \, 400 = slow. Breathing at 1 Hz: the kick rushes and drags every second. Kick preset CH: rolls. Open [pd drum-voices] and retune the kick (65 Hz)., f 90;
#X obj 700 96 cnv 1 570 554 empty empty THE\ DRUMS 8 12 0 13 #fff1e0 #1d3557 0;
#N canvas 40 60 1000 480 drum-voices 0;
#X text 20 10 KICK: every kick spike (one sample of 1.0) rings a [bob~] ladder filter tuned to 65 Hz \, just below self-oscillation. HAT: every burst spike crosses [threshold~] and fires a 40 ms noise burst through a highpass., f 130;
#X obj 20 60 r~ \$0-kickspk;
#X obj 400 60 r~ \$0-hatspk;
#X obj 20 120 bob~;
#X obj 160 70 loadbang;
#X msg 160 96 65;
#X msg 210 96 3.9;
#X obj 20 150 *~ 150;
#X obj 400 100 threshold~ 0.5 5 0.5 5;
#X msg 400 130 1 \, 0 40;
#X obj 400 156 vline~;
#X obj 400 182 *~;
#X obj 560 130 noise~;
#X obj 560 156 hip~ 6000;
#X obj 400 210 *~;
#X obj 400 236 *~ 0.25;
#X obj 20 270 hip~ 10;
#X obj 20 300 clip~ -1 1;
#X obj 20 330 outlet~;
#X connect 1 0 3 0;
#X connect 4 0 5 0;
#X connect 5 0 3 1;
#X connect 4 0 6 0;
#X connect 6 0 3 2;
#X connect 3 0 7 0;
#X connect 2 0 8 0;
#X connect 8 0 9 0;
#X connect 9 0 10 0;
#X connect 10 0 11 0;
#X connect 10 0 11 1;
#X connect 12 0 13 0;
#X connect 13 0 14 0;
#X connect 11 0 14 1;
#X connect 14 0 15 0;
#X connect 7 0 16 0;
#X connect 15 0 16 0;
#X connect 16 0 17 0;
#X connect 17 0 18 0;
#X restore 720 130 pd drum-voices;
#X text 860 130 <- the drum sounds (open), f 30;
#X obj 720 170 output~;
#X text 720 234 volume (turns DSP on), f 22;
#X obj 720 270 nn.spectrum~;
#X text 720 400 KICK: every kick spike rings a [bob~] filter at 65 Hz. HAT: every burst fires a short noise burst. No sequencer \, no clock: the neurons ARE the groove., f 64;
